// expect: 0
// A complete call with no arguments standing as a stage is applied whole:
// `mk()` answers a function, and the pipe hands 5 to it, so the program
// answers mk()(5) - 6, which is 0. Pin 47767c1238b2 read `mk` as a callee
// whose parameters were not known yet, judged `mk(5)`, and refused it.
fn mk() = { v => v + 1 }

fn main() = (5 |> mk()) - 6
